  service_history: Nagatsuki (長月, "September") was one of twelve Mutsuki-class destroyers,
    built for the Imperial Japanese Navy (IJN) during the 1920s. During the Pacific
    War, she participated in the Philippines Campaign in December 1941 and the Dutch
    East Indies Campaign in early 1942. In March, she was assigned to convoy escort
    duties in and around Malaysia and the Dutch East Indies until she was transferred
    to Rabaul in early 1943 to ferry troops around New Guinea and the Solomon Islands.
